    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">AMA UNIVERSITY PROGRAMS</h3>
    <p>GLE partners with the American Management Association (AMA) to offer more than 75 courses and five certificate programs for:</p>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="ama_programs.program_1">{{ ama_programs.program_1 }}</span></li>
        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="ama_programs.program_2">{{ ama_programs.program_2 }}</span></li>
        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="ama_programs.program_3">{{ ama_programs.program_3 }}</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>GLE offers AMA curriculum delivered by experienced faculty that meets the needs of professionals who want to enhance their management thinking and best practices.</p>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">Ed2Go</h3>
    <p>Through a partnership with Ed2Go, UOG GLE is able to offer more than 100 comprehensive trainings and career programs virtually that facilitate learning and workforce development.</p>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">English Adventure Program</h3>
    <p>The English Adventure Program is a short-term English language learning program designed for travel agents, students from visiting schools, and visiting institutions that want to learn English while enjoying the wonders of Guam's tropical vacation environment. The program offers a variety of packages tailored to meet the needs of each individual group. Custom packages can focus on beginning, intermediate, or advanced English curriculum. Optional tours, sports, cultural activities, and recreational activities may also be provided.</p>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">English Language Institute</h3>
    <div class="contact-info">
        <p>Location: <span data-field="english_language_institute.location">{{ english_language_institute.location }}</span></p>
        <p>Tel: <span data-field="english_language_institute.tel">{{ english_language_institute.tel }}</span></p>
        <p>Website: <span data-field="english_language_institute.website">{{ english_language_institute.website }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <p>The English Language Institute (ELI) at the University of Guam has offered classes in English as a Second</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="header-logo">
        <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="University of Guam Logo" style="height: 60px;"/>
        <h1 style="font-size: 24pt; margin-top: 5px;">UNIVERSITY OF GUAM</h1>
        <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 0;">UNIBETSEDAT GUÁHAN</h2>
    </div>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">UOG LAND GRANT EXTENSION SERVICE (Continued)</h3>
    <p>Extension is a key function of Land Grant universities that serves the needs of the community. The UOG Extension & Outreach (C&EO) programs under the College of Agriculture & Life Sciences (CALS) empower the multicultural community of Guam with more information, knowledge, and skills to improve their lives. C&EO provides direct programs and materials. Both in-person and online resources are available to all members of the community, and education venues that allow citizens of Guam and the surrounding region to learn about agriculture, food, and other needs are communicated to University professionals to answer questions through research.</p>
    <p>C&EO is part of a much larger family of 112 U.S. Land Grant Colleges and universities that share research, information, scientific breakthroughs, and best educational practices. C&EO is a major part of the University's efforts to improve the quality of life for the people of Guam and the region. As a bridge from the start-up phase, the Guam Small Business Development Center (SBDC) provides the long-term resources and support for students who have already launched their businesses. The added benefit is that students can remain plugged into both centers' networks for ongoing resources and support.</p>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">ISLA CENTER FOR THE ARTS</h3>
    <div class="contact-info">
        <p>Coordinator: <span data-field="isla_center_for_the_arts.coordinator_name">{{ isla_center_for_the_arts.coordinator_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Location: <span data-field="isla_center_for_the_arts.location">{{ isla_center_for_the_arts.location }}</span></p>
        <p>Tel: <span data-field="isla_center_for_the_arts.tel">{{ isla_center_for_the_arts.tel }}</span></p>
        <p>Website: <span data-field="isla_center_for_the_arts.website">{{ isla_center_for_the_arts.website }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <p>The mission of Isla Center for the Arts is to provide specialized programs in the arts that are not otherwise available to the community of Guam. The Center offers a variety of programs to conserve and promote the indigenous arts of the Pacific area and to serve as a source for a broad understanding of Western art and culture.</p>
    <p>Programming at Isla includes an annual series of exhibitions, free of charge, that emphasize the arts of the Pacific region as well as those of the Western world. Isla houses a permanent collection of more than 300 objects, including indigenous art, artifacts, and cultural items from the Pacific and Asia. The collection is the array of objects that represent the cultural and artistic heritage of the region. Objects in the collection are available for research upon request.</p>
    <p>Isla serves students ranging from elementary through university levels, local artists, the Guam public, and visitors to Guam. Isla's broad range of programming attracts approximately 2,500 patrons annually.</p>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">OFFICE OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY</h3>
    <div class="contact-info">
        <p>Chief Information Officer: <span data-field="office_of_information_technology.cio_name">{{ office_of_information_technology.cio_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Location: <span data-field="office_of_information_technology.location">{{ office_of_information_technology.location }}</span></p>
        <p>Tel: <span data-field="office_of_information_technology.tel">{{ office_of_information_technology.tel }}</span></p>
        <p>Email: <span data-field="office_of_information_technology.email">{{ office_of_information_technology.email }}</span></p>
        <p>Website: <span data-field="office_of_information_technology.website">{{ office_of_information_technology.website }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <p>The Office of Information Technology (OIT) provides a wide variety of academic, instructional, administrative, and research-related services. OIT supports these services by providing technology, hardware, software, and network and internet connectivity. Consistent with the regional role of the University, OIT also provides technical services and support to various public agencies as needed.</p>
    <p>The campus network is supported by a 10 GB Research & Education Network (REN), which provides high-speed internet access, and connectivity to internet exchange points. OIT provides network and internet access throughout the campus utilizing monitored wired and wireless networks. OIT also provides the availability of open research & education exchange (GOREX) link with the University of Hawaii, authorized users can access internet resources from the University of Hawaii and other institutions between institutions and direct access to supported content delivery networks.</p>
    <p>Additionally, the University of Guam participates in EduRoam, a global roaming service that allows students and participating institutions to securely access the campus network using their own institution's credentials.</p>
    <p>The University of Guam Computer Labs are equipped with modern computer workstations, printers, and multimedia software such as Microsoft Office, Google Suite, statistical analysis software, and high-speed internet access. CAD and GIS software are available upon request.</p>
    <p>The Computer Labs are located at:</p>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="computer_labs.location_1">{{ computer_labs.location_1 }}</span></li>
        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="computer_labs.location_2">{{ computer_labs.location_2 }}</span></li>
        <li class="list-item"><span data-field="computer_labs.location_3">{{ computer_labs.location_3 }}</span></li>
    </ul>
</div>

