    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">PACIFIC ISLANDS SMALL BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT CENTER NETWORK / GUAM SMALL BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT CENTER</h3>
    <div class="contact-info">
        <p>Director: <span data-field="pacific_islands_sbdc.director_name">{{ pacific_islands_sbdc.director_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Location: <span data-field="pacific_islands_sbdc.location">{{ pacific_islands_sbdc.location }}</span></p>
        <p>Tel: <span data-field="pacific_islands_sbdc.tel">{{ pacific_islands_sbdc.tel }}</span></p>
        <p>Email: <span data-field="pacific_islands_sbdc.email">{{ pacific_islands_sbdc.email }}</span></p>
        <p>Website: <span data-field="pacific_islands_sbdc.website">{{ pacific_islands_sbdc.website }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <p>The Pacific Islands Small Business Development Center Network (PIISBDC) is a part of the University of Guam School of Business & Public Administration. It was established to coordinate resources from the University of Guam, the local government, the federal government, and the private sector to provide high-quality business and economic development assistance to existing and prospective small businesses.</p>
    <p>PIISBDC contracts with local agencies to establish service centers that provide high-quality management and technical assistance to current and potential small business owners. Assistance is provided through counseling programs, training programs, business and economic development, and other programs. The center also works with other minority programs, veterans programs, village programs, and other community programs. The center also provides business assistance center program, and an international trade program.</p>
    <p>Existing service centers under the PIISBDC include the Guam Small Business Development Center (GSBDC) and SBDCs in the Federated States of Micronesia (FSM), Palau, and the Marshall Islands. Advisors within these service centers provide direct assistance and coordinate the clients</p>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">ROBERT F. KENNEDY MEMORIAL LIBRARY</h3>
    <div class="contact-info">
        <p>Dean of University Libraries: <span data-field="rfk_library.dean_name">{{ rfk_library.dean_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Tel: <span data-field="rfk_library.tel">{{ rfk_library.tel }}</span></p>
        <p>Reference Desk: <span data-field="rfk_library.reference_desk_tel">{{ rfk_library.reference_desk_tel }}</span></p>
        <p>Website: <span data-field="rfk_library.website">{{ rfk_library.website }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <p>The Territorial College of Guam Library was founded in 1952, the same year the Territorial College of Guam was established. The curriculum of the College of Guam Library has evolved to meet the needs of the community and public libraries on Guam. Since then, the University of Guam has expanded its library services to include a comprehensive collection of materials that supports the academic and research needs of the University and the community.</p>
    <p>The RFK Memorial Library is an academic component and the central library facility of the University. At present, it houses more than 98,059 print titles and 124,977 print holdings; 26,902 microfilm reels and 899,748 microfiche units; 1,527 print serial titles; 187,897 print serial issues; and 5,289 multimedia items.</p>
</div>

