    </div>

    <h3 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">INTEGRATED LIBRARY SYSTEM (ILS)</h3>
    <p>The Integrated Library System (ILS) was installed in January 2009, and SYMPHONY went live in February 2009. The library's online catalog, OCEAN, allows 24/7 access to library resources. Users can search the catalog for books, journals, and other electronic resources, both on and off campus. Electronic database resources subscribed by and licensed to the University are accessible to users from any location with an internet connection, provided they are properly authenticated.</p>
    <p>In September 2009, the Library received a three-year Federal National Leadership Grant from the Institute of Museum and Library Services for Future Island Projects. For Future Island Projects, the library has been able to acquire new electronic resources, research assistance for theses and special projects, and other resources that support the academic needs of the University.</p>
    <p>The RFK Memorial Library was designated a Selective Federal Depository in 1978 through the University's land-grant status. As one of the two selective depository libraries in the region, the library provides free access to federal government publications and materials.</p>
    <p>Other special collections at the RFK Memorial Library include the Mobil East Asian Collection, the Thesis and Special Projects Collection, the Micronesian Resource File, and the Reference Information File consisting of local and ephemeral materials of current interest. The East Asia Collection offers books and periodicals on the cultures, history, language, and societies of Japan, Korea, China, Taiwan, and Hong Kong. Mobil Oil also has a collection of materials on the oil industry and continued support.</p>
    <p>The Instructional Media Services within the Library serves student and faculty needs in audio-video duplication and video projects.</p>
